\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. We saw Thee not when Thou didst come
\par To this poor world of sin and death,
\par Nor e'er beheld Thy cottage home
\par In that despised Nazareth;
\par But we believe Thy footsteps trod
\par Its streets and plains, Thou Son of God.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. We did not see Thee lifted high 
\par Amid that wild and savage crew,
\par Nor heard Thy meek, imploring cry;
\par Forgive, they know not what they do
\par Ye we believe the deed was done,
\par Which shook the earth and veiled the sun.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. We stood not by the empty tomb
\par Where late Thy sacred body lay,
\par Nor sat within that upper room,
\par Nor met Thee in the open way
\par But we believe that angels said
\par Why seek the living with the dead?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. We did not mark the chosen few, 
\par When Thou didst through the clouds ascend,
\par First lift to heaven their wondering view,
\par Then to the earth all prostrate bend;
\par Yet we believe that mortal eyes
\par Beheld that journey to the skies.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. And now that Thou dost reign on high,
\par And thence Thy waiting people bless
\par No ray of glory from the sky
\par Doth shine upon our wilderness;
\par But we believe Thy faithful word,
\par And trust in our redeeming Lord.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

